Hi, all! I've been away a bit, for various reasons, but I've recently
been fooling around with the latest version of SLASH 'EM. I've noticed
a couple changes in the recent version that haven't been updated in
Eva's spoilers, most notably with #twoweaponing. (Er, of course it's
possible that these aren't actually changes and instead are just
things I've never noticed.)

First, #twoweaponing artifacts seems to have changed. Off-hand
artifacts still retain offensive special powers (confirmed with Fire
Brand and Stormbringer in wizard mode), but lose defensive powers
(confirmed with Excalibur and Grayswander), including automatic
searching. Only the primary-hand weapon grants defensive special
abilities. This is true regardless of whether your other weapon is an
artifact or not.

Also, it seems you can #twoweapon your hand as a second weapon while
wielding a main weapon, which is pretty cool.

Seems fair enough to me. I've fired off a note to Eva, in case she
wants to update, but for hysterical raisins and all like that I
thought I should post something. Do feel free to correct me if I've
just been oblivious to this feature in the past.

